[/tikz]
(a) Represent the network as an adjacency table.
(b) Explain why the table is symmetrical.

The arrows show direct journeys. The weights are journey times in minutes.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta,decorations.markings}
\tikzset{midarrow/.style={decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.55 with {\arrow{Stealth[length=3mm]}}},postaction={decorate}}}
\coordinate (A) at (0,2.4);
\coordinate (B) at (3.2,2.4);
\coordinate (C) at (0,0);
\coordinate (D) at (3.2,0);
\draw[midarrow] (A) to[bend left=22] node[pos=0.3,above] {$12$} (B);
\draw[midarrow] (B) to[bend left=22] node[pos=0.3,below] {$27$} (A);
\draw[midarrow] (A) -- (C) node[midway,left] {$35$};
\draw[midarrow] (C) -- (B) node[midway,sloped,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$46$};
\draw[midarrow] (B) -- (D) node[midway,right] {$58$};
\draw[midarrow] (D) -- (C) node[midway,below] {$69$};
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt);
\node[above left] at (A) {$A$};
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt);
\node[above right] at (B) {$B$};
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt);
\node[below left] at (C) {$C$};
\fill (D) circle (2.5pt);
\node[below right] at (D) {$D$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(a) Represent the directed network as an adjacency table.
(b) Explain why the table is not symmetrical along the diagonal.

examples.solution_text:
Draw the four vertices $P$, $Q$, $R$ and $S$.
Use the row as the starting point and the column as the finishing point of each arrow.
Row $P$ gives $P\to Q$ with weight $14$ and $P\to R$ with weight $23$.
Row $Q$ gives $Q\to P$ with weight $36$ and $Q\to S$ with weight $47$.
Row $R$ gives $R\to Q$ with weight $58$.
Row $S$ gives $S\to R$ with weight $69$.
Draw no other connections.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta,decorations.markings}
\tikzset{midarrow/.style={decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.55 with {\arrow{Stealth[length=3mm]}}},postaction={decorate}}}
\coordinate (P) at (0,2.4);
\coordinate (Q) at (3.2,2.4);
\coordinate (R) at (0,0);
\coordinate (S) at (3.2,0);
\draw[midarrow] (P) to[bend left=22] node[pos=0.3,above] {$14$} (Q);
\draw[midarrow] (Q) to[bend left=22] node[pos=0.3,below] {$36$} (P);
\draw[midarrow] (P) -- (R) node[midway,left] {$23$};
\draw[midarrow] (R) -- (Q) node[midway,sloped,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {$58$};
\draw[midarrow] (Q) -- (S) node[midway,right] {$47$};
\draw[midarrow] (S) -- (R) node[midway,below] {$69$};
\fill (P) circle (2.5pt);
\node[above left] at (P) {$P$};
\fill (Q) circle (2.5pt);
\node[above right] at (Q) {$Q$};
\fill (R) circle (2.5pt);
\node[below left] at (R) {$R$};
\fill (S) circle (2.5pt);
\node[below right] at (S) {$S$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
